    { q: 'How does Sparkplug B work on MQTT?', a: 'Sparkplug B puts a structure on MQTT topics and payloads, with births that announce what a node has, deaths when it goes away, and sequence numbers that let a host notice a gap and ask for a rebirth. HotLoop implements both sides.' },
    { q: 'What is a unified namespace?', a: 'A unified namespace is a single, structured place, usually an MQTT broker, where every machine and system publishes its data under a consistent naming scheme, so anything that needs a value reads it from there and not from the device.' },
